---
const rows: [string, string, string, string][] = [
  ["How models are made", "A neural model generates a mesh from a prompt or an image", "The agent drives Blender step by step through tool calls", "The agent writes a source file in a text notation that KILN compiles"],
  ["Models are stored as", "Meshes (.glb, .fbx)", ".blend files", "Text in git: diffable, reviewable, editable by hand or by agent"],
  ["Cost / access", "Cloud credits or a subscription; open-weight models need a large GPU", "Free; needs Blender installed", "Free, MIT, offline, CPU only"],
  ["Meshes", "Dense or uneven triangles; often needs clean-up", "Whatever the agent builds", "Closed meshes within the style's triangle budget, LODs on request"],
  ["Style across a game", "Per prompt / reference image", "None built in", "Project-wide styles and palettes; change one, every model follows"],
  ["Rigs and animation", "Auto-rigging on some services, mostly humanoids", "Possible, by hand", "Pivots, rigid or soft skins, poses and cycles in the notation"],
  ["Quality checks", "None", "None built in", "A linter and previews the agent reads, so it fixes its own mistakes"],
  ["Engine output", "glTF / FBX", "Whatever Blender exports", "glTF + manifest.json for any engine; Godot scenes, materials and look kits"],
  ["Deterministic", "No", "Depends on the agent", "Yes: same text, same model"],
];
---

<section id="compare">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">How it compares</span>
    <h2>Three ways to get 3D from an agent</h2>
    <p class="lede">Facts as of October 2026. Pick what fits your game.</p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Image / text-to-3D generators<small>Meshy, Tripo, Rodin, Hunyuan3D</small></th>
            <th scope="col">Agent-driven Blender<small>Blender MCP servers</small></th>
            <th scope="col" class="us">KILN</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            rows.map(([k, a, b, c]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{k}</th>
                <td>{a}</td>
                <td>{b}</td>
                <td class="us">{c}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="where">
      <b>Where KILN loses:</b> it isn't a sculptor. Realistic or finely detailed models (faces, hands, foliage) are
      beyond simple blended shapes: use a CC0 pack or a generator for those. KILN wins on a whole game's worth of
      stylised models that match, move and stay maintainable.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-top: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 760px;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  thead th {
    font: 600 0.95rem var(--font-display);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  thead small {
    display: block;
    font: 0.75rem var(--font-body);
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  tbody th {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    width: 15%;
  }
  td {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .us {
    color: var(--text);
    background: rgba(224, 103, 60, 0.08);
  }
  thead .us {
    color: var(--glow);
  }
  tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .where {
    margin-top: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .where b {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
